{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486106670,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMDUwODg5Mzc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1251","origin":"github"},"title":"Git-annex bundled Git may not behave like system Git (i.e. hooks/ directory missing)","message":"TL;DR:\n\n\u003e I suspect that Git from git-annex only comes with the actual tools, but not all the convenience grease. `hooks/` content is typically just sample files by default, and I guess they just aren't available.\n\u003e So we should not assume that things have to look identical.\n\n\nIn #1237 we see weird behavior of `git init` that inits a repo without creating the complete set of usual directories under `.git/`. Here is how to get this outside datalad:\n\n````\n% ssh localhost 'mkdir /tmp/s3; git -C /tmp/s3 init'\nInitialized empty Git repository in /tmp/s3/.git/\n% tree -d s3/.git\ns3/.git\n├── branches\n├── hooks\n├── info\n├── objects\n│   ├── info\n│   └── pack\n└── refs\n    ├── heads\n    └── tags\n\n% ssh localhost 'export \"PATH=/usr/lib/git-annex.linux:$PATH\"; mkdir /tmp/s5; git -C /tmp/s5 init'\nInitialized empty Git repository in /tmp/s5/.git/\n% tree -d s5/.git\ns5/.git\n├── objects\n│   ├── info\n│   └── pack\n└── refs\n    ├── heads\n    └── tags\n````\n\nneeds no SSH to get there:\n\n````\n% export \"PATH=/usr/lib/git-annex.linux:$PATH\"; mkdir /tmp/s8; git -C /tmp/s8 init\nInitialized empty Git repository in /tmp/s8/.git/\ntree -d s8/.git\ns8/.git\n├── objects\n│   ├── info\n│   └── pack\n└── refs\n    ├── heads\n    └── tags\n````\n\nGit versions are both recent-ish but not identical.\n\n````\n% export \"PATH=/usr/lib/git-annex.linux:$PATH\"; git --version\ngit version 2.10.2\n% /usr/bin/git --version\ngit version 2.11.0\n````\n\nAfter upgrading git-annex to 6.20170101+gitg93d69b1-1~ndall+1 the version is identical, but the behavior still isn't.\n\n````\n% export \"PATH=/usr/lib/git-annex.linux:$PATH\"; git --version\ngit version 2.11.0\n% export \"PATH=/usr/lib/git-annex.linux:$PATH\"; mkdir /tmp/s9; git -C /tmp/s9 init\nInitialized empty Git repository in /tmp/s9/.git/\n% tree -d s9/.git\ns9/.git\n├── objects\n│   ├── info\n│   └── pack\n└── refs\n    ├── heads\n    └── tags\n````","files":null}]}